              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lǚtú is built from 旅 'to travel' and tú 'a road', both inherited from Middle Chinese, ljoX and du (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary glosses the first as a body of troops and the second 'a road'."
